# A comma inside a parenthesized right table (M1-19).
mode: syntax
---- query
T | join (U | where a, b) on k
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..31
  PIPELINE@0..30
    NAME_REF@0..1
      IDENT@0..1 "T"
    WHITESPACE@1..2 " "
    PIPE@2..3 "|"
    WHITESPACE@3..4 " "
    JOIN_OP@4..30
      IDENT@4..8 "join"
      WHITESPACE@8..9 " "
      PAREN_EXPR@9..25
        L_PAREN@9..10 "("
        PIPELINE@10..24
          NAME_REF@10..11
            IDENT@10..11 "U"
          WHITESPACE@11..12 " "
          PIPE@12..13 "|"
          WHITESPACE@13..14 " "
          WHERE_OP@14..24
            IDENT@14..19 "where"
            WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
            NAME_REF@20..21
              IDENT@20..21 "a"
            COMMA@21..22 ","
            WHITESPACE@22..23 " "
            NAME_REF@23..24
              IDENT@23..24 "b"
        R_PAREN@24..25 ")"
      WHITESPACE@25..26 " "
      IDENT@26..28 "on"
      WHITESPACE@28..29 " "
      NAME_REF@29..30
        IDENT@29..30 "k"
  WHITESPACE@30..31 "\n"

error[DS0115]: `where` takes one condition
  --> query:1:22
  |
1 | T | join (U | where a, b) on k
  |                      ^ a comma does not join conditions
  |
  = help: combine the conditions with `and`: `a and b`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    T | join (U | where a and b) on k
which parses without errors
